WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:07.620
The most special day of the year is our Birthday!

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.020
And birthday gets with it a delicious birthday cake!

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.870
But what if cakes were never so delicious and fluffy?

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.420
Well the fluffiness is all thanks to the YEAST

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.120
that helps it get spongy!

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:22.780
But the yeast is just so tiny!

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.160
And how can it help us so much?

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.220
Well, there are several organisms tinier than

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.300
yeast that help us to obtain many useful products.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.380
These little creatures are called MICRO-ORGANISMS!

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.324
Now as the name says, Micro means very small

00:00:40.324 --> 00:00:43.420
or microscopic structures, while organisms

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:44.740
are living beings.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.914
Thus, those organisms which cannot be observed

00:00:48.914 --> 00:00:51.600
with naked eyes, and require a microscope

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.240
to be seen, are the Micro-organisms.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.580
These tiny creatures come in various shapes,

00:00:58.580 --> 00:00:59.780
forms, and structures.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:03.340
For studying them, a proper categorisation

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.380
is really necessary.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.875
Thus, we classify these micro-organisms, simply

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.940
referred to as microbes, in four major classes:

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.000
Bacteria, Fungi, Protozoa and Algae.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.840
Let’s get introduced to each.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.520
Let us begin with Bacteria first.

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:27.419
They are usually unicellular prokaryotic organisms.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.700
What do we mean by this?

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:32.000
Unicellular as the name suggests, are made

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.540
up of single cell . So the entire body of

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:38.300
the organism consists of just one cell?

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:39.920
Yes!

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.700
That is how it is!

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.060
And what do we mean by Prokaryotic?

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.540
Well, the word arises from two Greek terms.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.700
The term “Pro” means “before” that

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.780
refers to Primitive form.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.155
Whereas the term “Karyon” means “kernel

00:01:54.155 --> 00:01:56.590
or nut” and here it refers to a membrane

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.980
bound nucleus.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:01.582
So Prokaryotic organisms are those which do

00:02:01.582 --> 00:02:04.900
not have a proper, well-defined nucleus . As

00:02:04.909 --> 00:02:08.585
we can see here , in these organisms the genetic

00:02:08.585 --> 00:02:11.160
material is randomly scattered in the cytoplasm.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:15.251
So when we say that Bacteria are unicellular

00:02:15.251 --> 00:02:18.310
prokaryotes, it means they have a single cell

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:20.760
which is of a primitive type, without a well-defined

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.860
nucleus.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.600
Would studying them be simpler then?

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.040
Not really!

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.960
Bacteria, in spite of their unicellular and

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.220
prokaryotic nature, come in diverse forms.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.300
They come in various shapes and sizes, and

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.660
are present almost everywhere around us.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.820
So how do we study so many types?

00:02:41.829 --> 00:02:43.379
It’s simple!

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:45.400
We classify them into categories.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:48.700
Based on their SHAPES, we classify them into

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.200
four major groups.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.362
As we can see here, the spherical ones called

00:02:55.362 --> 00:02:56.600
Coccus , or plural Cocci.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.820
Then these rod-shaped ones called Bacillus

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.620
or plural Bacilli.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.620
Then we have these comma-shaped bacteria called

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.420
Vibrio , plural Vibrios.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:11.890
And lastly, we have these spiral shaped ones

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.140
called the Spirillum or plural Spirilla.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:16.980
There are numerous other ways of classifying

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:17.840
the bacteria.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:21.320
However, we restrict ourselves to only this

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.460
one simple type: based on shapes!

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.120
Now where do you think these bacteria will be found?

00:03:27.129 --> 00:03:28.819
In isolated places?

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:31.629
Or scattered at specific points?

00:03:31.629 --> 00:03:33.560
Will they be found only on land?

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.250
Or only in water?

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.100
Or both?

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.830
Well there is single word which describes

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:41.440
their presence; and that word is “EVERYWHERE

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.000
”! Yes!

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:46.180
There is no single place on this earth where

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:47.280
you won’t find bacteria!

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.540
May it be the hot springs, or the ice cladded regions.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:55.440
May it be the salty Dead Sea, or even the marshy lands.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.020
They are present everywhere!

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:00.180
And let me tell you an amazing fact!

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.900
Some of them are even present inside you!

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:05.319
But don’t worry!

00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:07.709
The ones inside you are like friends!

00:04:07.709 --> 00:04:11.029
They won’t harm you in any way!

00:04:11.029 --> 00:04:13.640
Well this was about the various types of bacteria in

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:14.200
short.

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.020
Now we need to take a look at the next category

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.000
of micro-organisms as well.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.940
Let’s talk about Fungi in the next video.

